@TraderStoc83476 They have no choice but to try and move upstream and thus take revenue from their own customers.

@michal_majka It’s very frustrating, and just undermines them every time, because it makes you want to look at alternatives every time it happens. 

Every model update tends to fully destroy workflows that worked well, with zero benefit.

@99redder Yes, but all of that output is extremely easy to migrate. You can even ask their own tools to do it for you.

@kevin980606 These labs are basically movie studios.

Well, people will pay for the model, but then move onto a better or cheaper model or feature said very easily. 

And every time they release a new model is a new opportunity to hop around (because the output from every model is truly dramatically different, and model changes also destroy workflows).

@kdpisda Yes. Having to rework prompts every time there is a small model update is absolutely insane. Such a waste of time. And yet you have to do it because the output is often completely different!

And as these model launches get more frequent, it’s a terrible productivity sink.

@moneyandmore72 Investors are herd animals.

